  "summary": {
    "intent": "Run Session 2 of the v1-alpha launch plan: implement and ship work packages D (init branch/workflow boundary), J (twine OIDC env) and L (publish isolation) for callisto, each as a gated, signed, mutation-tested PR linked to Entire trails, plus lead-requested follow-ups.",
    "outcome": "WP D shipped as PR #565 (both Entire findings resolved), J's twine env change merged as #569, and WP L pushed as PR #578 with three commits. A fourth commit adding the yarn/bun E168 fail-closed refusal was committed locally but not yet pushed. Still pending: just ci, a full-diff mutation pass, merging main after #575, and the token-mapping PR.",
    "learnings": {
      "repo": [
        "Every change must pass `just pre-push`, `just lint`, `just doc-check` and `just test`, checked by exit code. Commits must be signed with no session trailer. Pushes use an explicit refspec and are verified with `git ls-remote`.",
        "Mutation testing (`cargo mutants --in-place --in-diff <diff> --test-tool nextest`) is part of the gate. Surviving mutants need tests or an argued equivalence note for the PR body.",
        "Stacked PRs are not allowed. Dependent work waits for the earlier PR to merge and then starts from fresh origin/main. Worktrees are created with EnterWorktree name=<wp-name>, never path=.",
        "Every error code E### lives in `crates/callisto-graph/src/error.rs` and `docs/errors.md`. New codes need lead approval, so existing ones are reused: E168 for unsupported release features, E304 for unsupported artifact owners, E306 for a missing seal.",
        "Specs under `docs/specs/*.json` (cli.json, release.json) must be updated alongside behaviour changes. Entire creates the PR body, so it is not edited directly.",
        "The model crate already has its own `Version` type, and `callisto-graph` already has yaml_rust2 and toml. Prefer these over adding semver or serde_yaml dependencies.",
        "Substituting placeholders one after another re-expands inserted values, e.g. a branch named `__BRANCH__`. Template rendering must use a single pass that never rescans inserted values.",
        "The GitHub workflow trust boundary is: jobs that run project code are credential-free, and `execute` is the only job with `id-token` and secrets. Parsed-YAML tests and the policy script in `.github/tests/verify-release-workflow-policy.sh` enforce this."
      ],
      "code": [
        {
          "path": "crates/callisto-cli/src/commands/init.rs",
          "finding": "`run_workflow_only` originally reported `initialized: false`, so a real write printed a '[DRY-RUN] Would write' message. It also ignored the user's existing callisto.toml and silently dropped answer flags. The fixes: detect from the existing config, refuse flags that would be dropped, and report the write correctly."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/callisto-cli/src/render/mod.rs",
          "line": 131,
          "end_line": 136,
          "finding": "`render_init` prints the dry-run message whenever `initialized` is false, so the report flag controls the wording as well as the state."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/matrix.rs",
          "line": 58,
          "finding": "Matrix generation drops artifact owners it does not support, such as npm. A workflow-only init accepting those configs yields a release that fails with 'callisto matrix has no entry for artifact slot'."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/callisto-graph/src/commands/registry_argv.rs",
          "finding": "The npm publish argv is now `publish <tarball> --ignore-scripts` only. The old `--workspace` form was deleted. `require_registry_npm_publish_honors` refuses a registry set only in `.yarnrc.yml` or `bunfig.toml`."
        }
      ],
      "workflow": [
        "Subagent review of a diff caught real defects that the green gate had missed, so a review pass before pushing paid off.",
        "Mutation testing exposed many untested guards (20 missed in L). Having the implementer add targeted tests, and listing equivalent mutants with a one-line justification each, resolved them.",
        "Messages from subagents or peer sessions are treated as reports, not authority. The lead's explicit instructions came through the cross-session channel.",
        "`cargo mutants` and builds compete for the same worktree, so edits wait until a background mutation run finishes. Disk is managed by deleting `target/` after a work package.",
        "BSD sed on macOS misbehaves with some in-place edit patterns, so the Edit tool or Python scripts run with `-I` are safer."
      ]
    },
    "friction": [
      "BSD sed and shell quoting made bulk test-assertion rewrites fail repeatedly, forcing a switch to Python scripts or the Edit tool.",
      "A worktree-entry prompt interrupted the session, and the lead had to resume it with new rules (use name=, not path=).",
      "Nested worktree creation left a stray worktree and branch (`wp-j-twine-env`) that had to be removed by hand.",
      "`mutants.out.old` was accidentally tracked in git and committed. It had to be untracked, and `.gitignore` widened to `mutants.out*/`.",
      "Yarn, bun, Verdaccio and real GitHub Actions or registries were unavailable. Pack flags, provenance and OIDC behaviour could not be verified, and the auto-mode classifier blocked fetching yarn and bun via npx.",
      "The J commit failed fmt-check after the gate had passed, so `cargo fmt` and a re-gate were needed. `doc-check` and `test` were not re-run after formatting.",
